---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia router BGP to support receiving link-bandwidth extended communities from EBGP peers for ipv4 address family?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia router to receive link-bandwidth extended communities from EBGP peers for the IPv4 address family, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. This configuration enables the router to accept and use link-bandwidth extended communities attached to IPv4 routes received from EBGP peers in the specified group.
