Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to enable receiving BGP Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) capabilities from a peer during extended community negotiation, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    outbound-route-filtering
        extended-community
            accept-orf
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration enables the router to negotiate the receive capability in BGP ORF with a peer and accept filters that the peer wishes to send. You can apply this at the global BGP level, group level, or neighbor level depending on your specific requirements.
