## User question:
"How to configure Nokia routers to automatically add a link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to automatically add a link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group <ebgp-group-name>
        type external
        link-bandwidth
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            peer-as <peer-as-number>
            import "add-link-bandwidth"
    exit
exit

configure router policy-options
    begin
    policy-statement "add-link-bandwidth"
        entry 10
            from protocol bgp
            action accept
                add-community "link-bandwidth:<bandwidth-value>"
            exit
        exit
    commit
exit
```

Replace:
- `<ebgp-group-name>` with your EBGP group name
- `<peer-ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address
- `<peer-as-number>` with the neighbor's AS number
- `<bandwidth-value>` with the desired bandwidth value in kbps (e.g., "100000" for 100 Mbps)

This configuration:
1. Creates an EBGP group with link-bandwidth capability
2. Applies an import policy that adds the link-bandwidth community to incoming BGP routes
3. Uses policy-options to define the community additi
