## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to automatically add a link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <EBGP_GROUP_NAME>
        type external
        link-bandwidth
        neighbor <PEER_IP_ADDRESS>
            peer-as <PEER_AS_NUMBER>
            import "LBW_POLICY"
exit

configure router policy-options
    begin
    policy-statement "LBW_POLICY"
        entry 10
            from protocol bgp
            action accept
                add-community "link-bandwidth:<VALUE>" 
            exit
        exit
    commit
exit
```

Replace:
- `<EBGP_GROUP_NAME>` with your EBGP group name
- `<PEER_IP_ADDRESS>` with the neighbor's IP address
- `<PEER_AS_NUMBER>` with the neighbor's AS number
- `<VALUE>` with the desired link bandwidth value (e.g., interface speed in bits/sec)

For multiple neighbors, apply the `link-bandwidth` configuration at either the group or individual neighbor level as needed.
