To enable best-external advertisement for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes in BGP on Nokia routers, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    family label-ipv6
    exit
```

This enables the labeled-unicast IPv6 address family in BGP, allowing the router to advertise best-external routes for this address family. 

For more granular control, you can also configure specific parameters under the BGP group or neighbor contexts if needed. For example:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    family label-ipv6
    exit
```

These commands will ensure your Nokia router supports and advertises best-external labeled-unicast IPv6 routes via BGP.
