Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to allow active /32 LDP FEC prefixes to be advertised to a BGP peer with an RFC 3107 label, regardless of existing BGP paths for the same prefix, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family label-ipv4
            advertise-ldp-prefix
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of your BGP peer. Ensure the `family label-ipv4` is enabled for the neighbor to support labeled-unicast IPv4 routes.
------------
