Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to advertise a long-lived stale time of 86400 seconds in BGP graceful restart LLGR capability, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    long-lived
        helper-override-stale-time 86400
    exit
exit
```

This configuration will set the LLGR stale-time to 86400 seconds (24 hours) in the BGP graceful restart capability advertisement.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to advertise a long-lived stale time of 86400 seconds in BGP graceful restart LLGR capability?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to advertise a long-lived stale time of 86400 seconds in BGP graceful restart LLGR capability, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    long-lived
        helper-override-stale-time 86400
    exit
exit
```

This configuration will set the LLGR stale-time to 86400 seconds (24 hours) in the BGP graceful restart capability advertisement.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
advertised-stale-time <seconds>
no advertised-stale-time
FuncDef:
This command sets the value of the long-lived stale time that is advertised by the router in its LLGR capability. When configured in the long-lived configuration context,advertised-stale-timeapplies to all AFI/SAFI in the advertised LLGR capability except for any AFI/SAFI with a family-specific override. A family-specific override is configured with theadvertised-stale-timecommand in afamilycontext.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'seconds', 'Info': 'Specifies the advertised long-lived stale time in seconds. Values-0 to 16777215.'}
