Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes received from EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration:
1. Enables acceptance of link-bandwidth extended communities from EBGP peers for IPv4 routes
2. Aggregates the bandwidth values from these communities when readvertising routes with next-hop-self

For complete functionality, ensure you also have appropriate multipath settings configured under `config>router>bgp` if you want to utilize multiple paths for load balancing.
