To configure TCP authentication using the keychain named "BGP_SECURE_KEYS" for BGP sessions on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    auth-keychain "BGP_SECURE_KEYS"
exit
```

If you need to apply the keychain to a specific BGP group or neighbor, use these variations:

For a BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    auth-keychain "BGP_SECURE_KEYS"
exit
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    auth-keychain "BGP_SECURE_KEYS"
exit
```
