## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP fast reroute for labeled-unicast IPv6 routes on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        label-ipv6 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables BGP add-paths capability for labeled-IPv6 routes
2. Sets a send limit of 8 paths per prefix (adjust this value as needed)
3. Enables the ability to receive multiple paths per prefix

For optimal fast reroute operation, you should also ensure proper next-hop resolution is configured for labeled-IPv6 routes:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv6
                    resolution-filter bgp
                    resolution-filter sr-policy
                exit
            exit
        exit
