Here are the CLI commands to enable BGP routing protocol on a Nokia router:

```
configure router
    router-id <router-id>
    bgp
        router-id <ip-address>
        enforce-first-as
        remove-private [limited] [skip-peer-as]
        group <group-name>
            peer-as <as-number>
            neighbor <ip-address>
                peer-as <as-number>
```

Replace the placeholders with your specific values:
- `<router-id>` - Your router's ID (e.g., 192.168.1.1)
- `<ip-address>` - The BGP router ID (typically same as router-id)
- `<group-name>` - Name for your BGP peer group
- `<as-number>` - Autonomous System number for your router
- `<ip-address>` under neighbor - IP address of the BGP peer

For basic BGP configuration, these commands establish the BGP process, set the router ID, create a peer group, and define neighbors. You may need to add additional parameters depending on your specific requirements (like address families, route policies, etc.).
