Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
Here are the CLI commands to configure a BGP group with route reflector cluster ID 192.168.10.1 and ORR location ID 8, allowing local fallback:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type internal
        cluster 192.168.10.1 orr-location 8 allow-local-fallback
        peer-as <AS-number>
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<AS-number>` with your autonomous system number. This configuration:
1. Creates an internal BGP group
2. Sets the route reflector cluster ID to 192.168.10.1
3. Configures ORR location ID 8 
4. Enables local fallback when no optimal routes are available
