To configure the BGP Connect Retry timer to 90 seconds on a Nokia router, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp connect-retry 90
```

This command sets the BGP Connect Retry timer to 90 seconds globally for all BGP sessions under the router context. You can also apply this setting at the group or neighbor level if needed:

For a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> connect-retry 90
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> connect-retry 90
```
