To configure BGP to suppress unstable route advertisements while maintaining convergence of stable routes in Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
configure router bgp
    min-route-advertisement 120
    purge-timer 15
exit
```

These commands:
1. Set the minimum route advertisement interval to 120 seconds (`min-route-advertisement 120`) to prevent rapid updates of unstable routes
2. Configure a 15-minute purge timer (`purge-timer 15`) to remove stale routes that haven't been refreshed

For more granular control, you can apply these settings at the group or neighbor level:

```bash
configure router bgp group PEER_GROUP
    min-route-advertisement 90
exit
```

The default keepalive timer (30 seconds) and hold timer (90 seconds) will maintain normal BGP session stability while these route advertisement controls are in effect.
