To originate a default BGP route (0.0.0.0/0) towards specific peers in a Nokia router's BGP configuration, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family ipv4
                default-route-originate
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of the specific peer you want to advertise the default route to. 

If you need to include additional attributes like route policy or community values when originating the default route, you would add those under the `neighbor` context as well.
