To prevent BGP peers from using 4-byte autonomous system numbers on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration command:

```
configure router bgp disable-4byte-asn
```

This command can be applied at three levels:
1. Globally for all BGP peers under `config>router>bgp`
2. For a specific BGP group under `config>router>bgp>group`
3. For an individual neighbor under `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor`

Choose the appropriate level based on where you want to enforce the restriction.
