To prevent BGP peers from using 4-byte autonomous system numbers on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    disable-4byte-asn
exit
```

Alternatively, you can apply this setting at the group or neighbor level if you want more granular control:

For a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    disable-4byte-asn
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    disable-4byte-asn
exit
```
