## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to strictly support IPv4 routing exchanges with BGP peer 192.0.2.1 without negotiating any new capabilities?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to strictly support IPv4 routing exchanges with BGP peer 192.0.2.1 without negotiating any new capabilities, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            disable-capability-negotiation
            peer-as <peer-as-number>
            family ipv4
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired BGP group name and `<peer-as-number>` with the actual AS number of the peer at 192.0.2.1. The `disable-capability-negotiation` command ensures no new capabilities will be negotiated, while the `family ipv4` command restricts the session to IPv4 routing exchanges only.
