To prevent all BGP routes from being installed into RTM and FIB on the base router instance, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    disable-route-table-install
exit
```

This command will disable the installation of both labeled and unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 BGP routes into the Routing Table Manager (RTM) and Forwarding Information Base (FIB).
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to prevent all BGP routes from being installed into RTM and FIB on a Nokia router's base router instance?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent all BGP routes from being installed into RTM and FIB on the base router instance, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    disable-route-table-install
exit
```

This command will disable the installation of both labeled and unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 BGP routes into the Routing Table Manager (RTM) and Forwarding Information Base (FIB).
---
