To enable dynamic BGP session configuration for a peer group on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        dynamic-neighbor
        peer-as <as-number>
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired peer group name and `<as-number>` with the autonomous system number of the remote peers. This configuration allows the specified peer group to accept dynamic BGP neighbor connections from any IP address within the configured peer AS range.
