To enable dynamic BGP session configuration for a peer group on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        dynamic-neighbor
            peer-range <ip-prefix/mask>
            peer-as <as-number>
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your peer group name, `<ip-prefix/mask>` with the IP address range for dynamic peers, and `<as-number>` with the autonomous system number of the dynamic peers.

For example:
```
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        dynamic-neighbor
            peer-range 192.168.10.0/24
            peer-as 65001
        exit
    exit
exit
```
