Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure BGP graceful restart to indicate support for NOTIFICATION messages when the peer also supports this capability, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    enable-notification
exit
```

This will enable the router to advertise support for NOTIFICATION messages in its graceful restart capability. If the peer also supports this capability, the session can be gracefully restarted when NOTIFICATION messages are exchanged.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router's BGP graceful restart to indicate support for NOTIFICATION messages when the peer also supports this capability?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP graceful restart to indicate support for NOTIFICATION messages when the peer also supports this capability, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    enable-notification
exit
```

This will enable the router to advertise support for NOTIFICATION messages in its graceful restart capability. If the peer also supports this capability, the session can be gracefully restarted when NOTIFICATION messages are exchanged.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
enable-notification
no enable-notification
FuncDef:
When this command is present, the graceful restart capability sent by this router indicates support for NOTIFICATION messages. If the peer also supports this capability then the session can be restarted gracefully (while preserving forwarding) if either peer needs to sends a NOTIFICATION message due to some type of event or error.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
