## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to import all received VPN-IP routes into the dummy VRF for BGP next-hop resolution without regard to route targets?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to import all received VPN-IP routes into a dummy VRF for BGP next-hop resolution without regard to route targets, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        vpn-apply-import
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family vpn
                        resolution-filter
                            bgp
                            sr-te
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables `vpn-apply-import` to apply base BGP import policies to VPN routes
2. Configures next-hop resolution for VPN routes under `labeled-routes > transport-tunnel > family vpn`
3. Includes both BGP and SR-TE tunnels in the resolution filter for next-hop resolution

The routes will be imported regardless of their route targets since we're not applying any RT-based filtering at the VRF level.
