To verify that the last ASN in the AS_PATH of all routes received from an EBGP peer matches the configured `peer-as` value, use the `enforce-first-as` command under the BGP group or neighbor configuration:

```
configure router bgp 
    group <group-name>
        type external
        peer-as <remote-as-number>
        enforce-first-as
```

or for a specific neighbor:

```
configure router bgp 
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            peer-as <remote-as-number>
            enforce-first-as
```

This ensures BGP checks the last ASN in the AS_PATH against the configured `peer-as` value for all received routes.
