## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to only accept labeled routes for BGP next-hop resolution when the transport tunnels are explicitly tagged with an admin-tag?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to only accept labeled routes for BGP next-hop resolution when transport tunnels are explicitly tagged with an admin-tag, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family ipv4
    enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging
exit
```

```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family ipv6
    enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging
exit
```

These commands ensure that only LSPs marked with an admin-tag will be considered for next-hop resolution of labeled IPv4 and IPv6 BGP routes.
