To configure the Nokia router to apply the "INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY" for controlling outbound BGP routes, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    export "INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY"
exit
```

This will apply the route policy to all outbound BGP routes. If you need to apply the policy to a specific BGP group or neighbor, use these variations:

For a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    export "INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY"
exit
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    export "INTERNAL-BGP-POLICY"
exit
```
