To apply the "INTERNAL-BGP" route policy for controlling outbound BGP routes, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    export "INTERNAL-BGP"
exit
```

If you need to apply this policy to a specific BGP group or neighbor instead of globally, use these variations:

For a BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    export "INTERNAL-BGP"
exit
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    export "INTERNAL-BGP"
exit
```
