## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to enable extended community-based BGP filtering in outbound route filtering?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure extended community-based BGP filtering for outbound route filtering on Nokia routers, you'll need to create and apply an export policy that matches specific extended communities. Here are the CLI commands:

```
# Create a policy statement to match extended communities
configure router policy-options
begin
    # Define your extended community values (example uses route-target)
    community my-extended-comms members target:64512:100
    
    # Create a policy to match these communities
    policy-statement filter-by-extcomm
        entry 10
            from community my-extended-comms
            action reject
        exit
        default-action accept
    exit

    # Alternatively, if you want to permit only routes with specific extended communities:
    policy-statement permit-specific-extcomm
        entry 10
            from community my-extended-comms
            action accept
        exit
        entry 20
            action reject
        exit
    exit
commit
exit

# Apply the policy to BGP neighbors/groups
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        export filter-by-extcomm   # or use permit-specific-extcomm
    exit
    # Or apply to specific neighbor
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            export filter-by-extcomm
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` and `<ip-address>` with your actual BGP group and neighbor details, and adjust the community values (`target:64512:100`) to match your specific extended community requirements.
