Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure Nokia routers for both IPv6 unicast (labeled) and EVPN address families in BGP:

```
configure router bgp
    family label-ipv6 evpn
exit
```

For more granular control at the group or neighbor level:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    family label-ipv6 evpn
exit
```

To enable additional features like multipath and next-hop resolution for labeled IPv6:
```
configure router bgp
    multipath 8
    ibgp-multipath
    next-hop-resolution labeled-routes
        transport-tunnel
            family label-ipv6
                resolution-filter bgp
            exit
        exit
        allow-static
    exit
exit
```

These commands will enable both labeled IPv6 unicast and EVPN address families in BGP while providing optimal routing capabilities.
