To configure next-hop-resolution options for VPN-IPv4 and VPN-IPv6 routes on a Nokia router when they are not imported into any VPRN service, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure
    router
        bgp
            next-hop-resolution
                labeled-routes
                    vpn-ipv4
                        resolution-type route-table
                    exit
                    vpn-ipv6
                        resolution-type route-table
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration sets the next-hop resolution for VPN-IPv4 and VPN-IPv6 routes to use the global route table when they are not imported into any VPRN service. The `resolution-type route-table` option ensures that the next-hop is resolved using the main routing table rather than any VPRN-specific tables.
