## Proposed answer:
To create a BGP peer group named "EU-West-1" on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group "EU-West-1"
exit
```

This creates a basic BGP peer group. You can then add additional parameters to the group as needed, such as `peer-as`, `type`, or other BGP settings. For example, to specify the peer AS and type:

```
configure router bgp
    group "EU-West-1"
        peer-as 64512
        type external
    exit
exit
