To create a BGP peer group named "Transit-Partners" in Nokia router CLI, use the following commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group "Transit-Partners"
exit
```

This creates a basic BGP peer group. You can then add additional parameters to the group as needed, such as setting the type (internal/external), enabling peer tracking, or configuring prefix limits. For example:

```
configure router bgp
    group "Transit-Partners"
        type external
        enable-peer-tracking
        prefix-limit ipv4 500000 threshold 90 idle-timeout 30
    exit
exit
