---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to locally impose an LLGR stale time of 3600 seconds when overriding a peer's advertised value, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart long-lived
    helper-override-stale-time 3600
exit
```

If you need to apply this override for specific address families, navigate to the family context under `long-lived` and configure it there. For example:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart long-lived family ipv4
    helper-override-stale-time 3600
exit
