To configure Nokia routers to immediately send BGP UPDATE messages when sessions are established with peers, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp initial-send-delay-zero
```

This can be applied at the global BGP level, group level, or neighbor level depending on your specific requirements. For example:
- Global BGP configuration: `configure router bgp initial-send-delay-zero`
- Group configuration: `configure router bgp group <group-name> initial-send-delay-zero`
- Neighbor configuration: `configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> initial-send-delay-zero`
