## User question:
How to configure BGP on a Nokia router to announce reachability information immediately after session establishment with peers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP on a Nokia router to announce reachability information immediately after session establishment with peers, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp initial-send-delay-zero
```

This command can be applied at the global BGP level, group level, or neighbor level depending on your specific requirements. For example, to apply it to a specific group:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> initial-send-delay-zero
```

Or to a specific neighbor:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> initial-send-delay-zero
