## User question:
"How to configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 paths per unlabeled IPv4 unicast prefix and negotiate to receive multiple routes per prefix?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia router to advertise up to 8 paths per unlabeled IPv4 unicast prefix and negotiate to receive multiple routes per prefix, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    multipath 8
    add-paths ipv4 send receive
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables BGP multipath with a maximum of 8 paths per prefix (`multipath 8`)
2. Configures BGP Add-Paths capability for IPv4 unicast to both send and receive multiple paths per prefix (`add-paths ipv4 send receive`)

The `multipath` command applies to all address families supporting ECMP, while the `add-paths` command specifically enables the negotiation of multiple paths for IPv4 unicast prefixes.
