## User question:
"How to configure the BGP keepalive timer to 60 seconds on a Nokia router?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the BGP keepalive timer to 60 seconds on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    keepalive 60
exit
```

This sets the BGP keepalive interval to 60 seconds globally for all BGP peers. If you need to set it for a specific group or neighbor, navigate to those contexts instead:

For a specific group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    keepalive 60
exit
```

For a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    keepalive 60
exit
---
