To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 labeled-unicast IPv4 paths per prefix and negotiate to receive multiple paths, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        label-ipv4 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables the BGP add-paths capability for labeled-unicast IPv4 routes, sets the maximum number of advertised paths to 8 per prefix, and negotiates the ability to receive multiple paths.
