Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enter the configuration context for setting up labeled route options in BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family label-ipv4|label-ipv6|vpn
```

This will place you in the correct context where you can configure next-hop resolution options for labeled routes. Choose either `label-ipv4`, `label-ipv6`, or `vpn` depending on which address family you need to configure.
