To enable the configuration context for handling the link-bandwidth extended community on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

For group-level configuration:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    link-bandwidth
```

For neighbor-specific configuration:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    link-bandwidth
```

Once in the link-bandwidth context, you can configure additional parameters such as `send-to-ebgp`, `add-to-received-ebgp`, `aggregate-used-paths`, or `accept-from-ebgp` as needed for your specific requirements.
