To enable the configuration context for handling the link-bandwidth extended community attached to specific BGP routes on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

For group-level configuration:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> link-bandwidth
```

For neighbor-level configuration:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> link-bandwidth
```

After entering the link-bandwidth context, you can configure specific actions like `send-to-ebgp`, `add-to-received-ebgp`, `aggregate-used-paths`, or `accept-from-ebgp` for the desired address families.
