To configure the Nokia router to use the interface named "core-link-1" as the source address for BGP communication within a group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        local-interface "core-link-1"
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group. This configuration ensures that all BGP sessions within this group will use the specified interface as their source address.
------------
