## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes with MED values derived from IGP cost, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    med-out igp-cost
exit
```

This command sets the MED value to the IGP cost of the corresponding IP prefix when advertising routes to BGP peers. You can apply this at the global BGP level, group level, or individual neighbor level depending on your specific requirements.
