To configure a Nokia router to retain all MP-BGP routes in RIB-IN without requiring route refresh messages after VPN route policy changes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    rib-management
exit
```

This configuration enables RIB management, which ensures that all MP-BGP routes are retained in RIB-IN even when route policies change, eliminating the need for route refresh messages.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to retain all MP-BGP routes in RIB-IN without requiring route refresh messages after VPN route policy changes?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to retain all MP-BGP routes in RIB-IN without requiring route refresh messages after VPN route policy changes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    rib-management
exit
```

This configuration enables RIB management, which ensures that all MP-BGP routes are retained in RIB-IN even when route policies change, eliminating the need for route refresh messages.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
mp-bgp-keep
no mp-bgp-keep
FuncDef:
As a result of enabling this command, route refresh messages are no longer needed, or issued when VPN route policy changes are made; RIB-IN will retain all MP-BGP routes.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
