To configure Nokia routers to retain all MP-BGP routes in RIB-IN without requiring route refresh messages after VPN route policy changes, enable the Route Target Constraint (RTC) address family and originate the default RTC route. Here are the necessary CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    family vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6 route-target
    group <group-name>
        family vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6 route-target
        default-route-target
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration ensures that all VPN routes are retained in RIB-IN and eliminates the need for route refresh messages when VPN route policies change.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to retain all MP-BGP routes in RIB-IN without requiring route refresh messages after VPN route policy changes?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to retain all MP-BGP routes in RIB-IN without requiring route refresh messages after VPN route policy changes, enable the Route Target Constraint (RTC) address family and originate the default RTC route. Here are the necessary CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    family vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6 route-target
    group <group-name>
        family vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6 route-target
        default-route-target
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration ensures that all VPN routes are retained in RIB-IN and eliminates the need for route refresh messages when VPN route policies change.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
mp-bgp-keep
no mp-bgp-keep
FuncDef:
As a result of enabling this command, route refresh messages are no longer needed, or issued when VPN route policy changes are made; RIB-IN will retain all MP-BGP routes.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
