To configure the TTL value to 32 for EBGP packets when the peer is multiple hops away on a Nokia router, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp
    multihop 32
exit
```

Alternatively, if you want to apply this setting to a specific BGP group or neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    multihop 32
exit
```

or

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    multihop 32
exit
```
