Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure your Nokia router to advertise up to 8 different paths per multicast VPN IPv4 prefix and negotiate receiving multiple paths from BGP peers, use these CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        family mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
    exit
    ibgp-multipath
exit
```

For specific BGP groups or neighbors where you want to apply this:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    add-paths
        family mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
    exit
exit

configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    add-paths
        family mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

These configurations will enable both sending and receiving multiple paths for MVPN IPv4 prefixes while maintaining iBGP multipath support.
