To configure a BGP peer with IP address 192.0.2.1 on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure
router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            peer-as <remote-as-number>
            type external
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired BGP group name and `<remote-as-number>` with the autonomous system number of the remote peer. The `type external` command indicates this is an EBGP peer; use `type internal` if it's an IBGP peer instead.
