To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes to a specific neighbor using the local BGP instance address as the next-hop, use the `next-hop-self` command under the neighbor configuration. Here's the CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip-address>
            next-hop-self
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip-address>` with the specific neighbor's IP address. This ensures all routes advertised to this neighbor will use the local BGP instance address as the next-hop.
