To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes using the local address as the next-hop for all routes within a specific group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        next-hop-self
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group. This configuration ensures that all routes advertised to peers within this group will use the local router's address as the next-hop.
