To configure a Nokia router to preserve BGP next-hop information for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes when advertising to peers in a specific group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        next-hop-unchanged label-ipv4 label-ipv6
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP peer group. This configuration ensures that the BGP next-hop remains unchanged for both labeled IPv4 and IPv6 routes when advertising to peers in the specified group.
