## User question:
How to enable optimal route reflection for BGP in Nokia router configuration?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable optimal route reflection (ORR) for BGP in a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    # Configure the ORR location ID (replace <location-id> with your desired value 1-16)
    optimal-route-reflection
        location <location-id>
    exit

    # Configure the cluster with ORR location ID (replace <cluster-id> with your RR cluster ID)
    cluster <cluster-id> orr-location <location-id>

    # Optionally enable local fallback if needed
    # cluster <cluster-id> orr-location <location-id> allow-local-fallback

    # Enable IBGP multipath for better path selection
    ibgp-multipath
exit
```

For each route reflector client, associate them with the ORR location by configuring them under the appropriate BGP group or neighbor context.
