To disable BGP session initiation attempts for a specific neighbor in a Nokia router, use the `passive` command under the neighbor configuration context. Here's the CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> passive
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the specific neighbor's IP address. This will prevent the router from initiating BGP connections to that neighbor while still allowing it to accept incoming connections.
