To enable automatic adjustment of TCP session MTU based on ICMP feedback in Nokia routers, use the following CLI configuration commands:

For BGP sessions:
```
configure router bgp
    path-mtu-discovery
exit
```

For specific BGP groups:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    path-mtu-discovery
exit
```

For specific BGP neighbors:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    path-mtu-discovery
exit
```

These commands enable Path MTU Discovery for the respective BGP sessions, which will automatically adjust the TCP session MTU based on ICMP feedback received from the network path.
