Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure the autonomous system number of 65530 for a remote BGP peer on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        peer-as 65530
        neighbor <remote-peer-ip-address>
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<remote-peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of your remote BGP peer.
