## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to tear down BGP sessions when the route to a neighbor address is not accepted by the policy named "core-routes", use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            prefix-limit ipv4 1 idle-timeout forever post-import
            import "core-routes"
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Sets a prefix limit of 1 for IPv4 routes with `post-import` flag to count only routes accepted by import policy
2. Configures the idle-timeout as forever to keep the session down until manually reset
3. Applies the "core-routes" import policy to the neighbor

If the "core-routes" policy rejects the neighbor's route, the session will be torn down permanently due to reaching the prefix limit (1 route) on post-import accepted routes.
