Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure your Nokia router to send a warning message when receiving 5000 IPv6 routes from a peer at an 80% threshold without terminating the BGP session, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family ipv6
                prefix-limit 5000 threshold 80 log-only
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of your BGP peer. This configuration will trigger a warning message when the peer reaches 4000 routes (80% of 5000) and again when reaching 5000 routes, while keeping the BGP session active.
------------
