To configure your Nokia router to accept dynamic BGP sessions from peers within the 192.168.10.0/24 subnet, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        type internal
        dynamic-neighbor
            prefix 192.168.10.0/24
        exit
        peer-as <your-local-AS-number>
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<your-local-AS-number>` with your actual autonomous system number. This configuration:
1. Creates a BGP group named "DYNAMIC_PEERS" 
2. Sets it as an internal (iBGP) group
3. Enables dynamic neighbor functionality
4. Specifies the 192.168.10.0/24 subnet from which to accept dynamic peers
5. Configures the expected peer AS number

Optionally, you may want to add these additional parameters to control scale and behavior:
```
configure router bgp
    dynamic-neighbor-limit <max-number-of-peers>
    purge-timer <minutes>
exit
```
