To configure the primary IPv4 address as 192.168.100.1 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    optimal-route-reflection
        location 1 primary-ip-address 192.168.100.1
    exit
exit
```

This configures location ID 1 with the specified primary IPv4 address for optimal route reflection. You can adjust the location ID (1-16) as needed for your topology.
