To configure the primary IPv6 address as 2001:db8::1 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    orr
        location
            primary-ipv6-address 2001:db8::1
```

This configures the specified IPv6 address as the primary address for BGP optimal route reflection under the location context.
