---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to automatically remove stale BGP VPN-IP routes after 15 minutes if they are not refreshed?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to automatically remove stale BGP VPN-IP routes after 15 minutes if they are not refreshed, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    purge-timer 15
exit
```

This sets the purge timer to 15 minutes (900 seconds), which will automatically remove stale VPN-IP routes if they are not refreshed within this timeframe.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
purge-timer <minutes>
no purge-timer
FuncDef:
When the system sends a VPN-IP Route-Refresh to a peer it sets all the VPN-IP routes received from that peer (in the RIB-IN) to stale and starts the purge-timer. If the routes are not updated (refreshed) before the purge-timer has expired then the routes are removed.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'minutes', 'Info': 'Specifies the maximum time before stale routes are purged. Values-1 to 60.'}
