## User question:
How to disable the delay in sending BGP withdrawals on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To disable the delay in sending BGP withdrawals on a Nokia router, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp rapid-withdrawal
``` 

This will enable immediate sending of BGP withdrawal messages without waiting for the Minimum Route Advertisement timer.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
rapid-withdrawal
no rapid-withdrawal
FuncDef:
This command disables the delay (Minimum Route Advertisement) on sending BGP withdrawals. Normal route withdrawals may be delayed up to the minimum route advertisement to allow for efficient packing of BGP updates.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
