Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure the resolution filter type for BGP next-hop resolution when using labeled routes with transport tunnel family settings:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family label-ipv4
    resolution-filter
        bgp
        enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging
    exit
exit
```

For label-ipv6:
```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family label-ipv6
    resolution-filter
        bgp
        enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging
    exit
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Enter the context for configuring BGP next-hop resolution for labeled routes
2. Configure the transport tunnel family (either label-ipv4 or label-ipv6)
3. Set the resolution filter to use BGP tunnels
4. Enable strict tunnel tagging enforcement
