Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure BGP next-hop resolution for labeled routes when transport tunnels are used in Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter bgp
                exit
                family ipv6
                    resolution-filter bgp
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

If you also need to allow static routes for next-hop resolution of labeled routes, add:
```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            allow-static
        exit
    exit
exit
```

These configurations enable BGP-labeled routes to resolve their next-hops through transport tunnels while optionally allowing static routes (excluding default routes) for next-hop resolution.
