## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP next-hop resolution to only bind to specific tunnel types in the resolution filter, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnel
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    [no] ldp
                    [no] bgp
                    [no] rib-api
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `[no]` with either the command (to enable) or `no` followed by the command (to disable) for each tunnel type you want to include/exclude from the resolution filter. For example, to only allow LDP tunnels:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnel
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    ldp
                    no bgp
                    no rib-api
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Similarly, for labeled routes (label-ipv4, label-ipv6, or vpn), use the transport-tunnel context instead:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        ldp
                        no bgp
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
