To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP graceful restart capability with a restart-time of 600 seconds, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    restart-time 600
exit
```

This will set the BGP graceful restart timer to 600 seconds globally for all BGP peers. If you need to configure it for a specific group or neighbor, navigate to the respective context (`config>router>bgp>group` or `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor`) and apply the same command under the `graceful-restart` sub-context.
