"How to configure Nokia routers to use RSVP tunnels with the best metric for BGP next-hop resolution?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to use RSVP tunnels with the best metric for BGP next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnels
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    rsvp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        rsvp
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration ensures that RSVP tunnels are prioritized for BGP next-hop resolution, selecting the tunnel with the best metric. The `rsvp` command under both `shortcut-tunnels` and `labeled-routes` contexts enables RSVP tunnel selection for IPv4 routes.
