To configure a secondary IPv4 address (192.168.10.20) for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        local-address 192.168.10.20
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This sets the local BGP session address to 192.168.10.20 for optimal route reflection operation.
