Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To add a secondary IPv4 address for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            local-address 192.168.10.20
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This configures the secondary local address for BGP peering.
