Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure the secondary IPv6 address 2001:db8::2 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor <neighbor-ipv6-address>
                local-address 2001:db8::2
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ipv6-address>` with the IPv6 address of the BGP neighbor. This will set the secondary IPv6 address as the local address for BGP communications with the specified neighbor.
