---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP ORF send capability for the extended community target `192.0.2.10:65535` on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    outbound-route-filtering extended-community
        send-orf target:192.0.2.10:65535
```

This configuration enables the router to negotiate the send capability for the specified extended community target in BGP ORF negotiations with the peer.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
send-orf [ <comm-id> ]
no send-orf [ <comm-id> ]
FuncDef:
This command instructs the router to negotiate the send capability in the BGP outbound route filtering (ORF) negotiation with a peer.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'comm-id', 'Info': 'Specifies up to 32 community policies, which must consist exclusively of route target extended communities. If it is not specified, then the ORF policy is automatically generated from configured route target lists, accepted client route target ORFs and locally configured route targets. Values-[target: {ip-address:comm-val | 2byte-asnumber:ext-comm-val | 4byte-asnumber:comm-val}.'}
