To configure BGP to include the link-bandwidth extended community in unlabeled unicast IPv6 routes advertised to EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type external
        family ipv6
        advertise-link-bandwidth
        neighbor <peer-ipv6-address>
            peer-as <peer-as-number>
```

Key points:
1. Ensure the group is configured as `type external` for EBGP
2. Enable IPv6 address family with `family ipv6`
3. Use the `advertise-link-bandwidth` command to include the bandwidth extended community
4. Configure the specific EBGP neighbor with their AS number

Note: The exact implementation may vary slightly depending on your specific Nokia router platform and software version. Some platforms might require additional parameters or have the command under different contexts.
