## User question:
"How to administratively disable a BGP neighbor on a Nokia router without removing its configuration?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To administratively disable a BGP neighbor on a Nokia router without removing its configuration, use the `shutdown` command under the specific neighbor context. Here’s the CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> shutdown
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This will disable the neighbor while preserving its configuration. To re-enable it later, use the `no shutdown` command.
---
