## User question:
How to prevent BGP routes from being reflected back to the sending peer on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent BGP routes from being reflected back to the sending peer on a Nokia router, use the `disable-client-reflect` command under the relevant BGP group or neighbor configuration. Here's the CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> disable-client-reflect
```

Or at the group level:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> disable-client-reflect
```

This will disable route reflection to the specified client(s), preventing routes from being reflected back to the originating peer.
