## User question:
How to prevent BGP routes from being reflected back to the originating peer on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent BGP routes from being reflected back to the originating peer on a Nokia router, use the `disable-client-reflect` command under the specific BGP neighbor or group configuration. Here's the CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            disable-client-reflect
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor within a group:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            disable-client-reflect
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This will ensure that routes learned from this neighbor are not reflected back to it.
