## User question:
How to configure Nokia router to allow BGP to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference IS-IS instance for next-hop resolution?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia router to allow BGP to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference IS-IS instance for next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        bgp
                        isis
                            preference 200
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables BGP next-hop resolution for labeled routes
2. Specifies IPv4 transport tunnels
3. Sets IS-IS tunnel preference to 200 (higher than default BGP preference of 170)
4. Includes both BGP and IS-IS in the resolution filter

The higher preference value for IS-IS ensures it will be selected last (lower priority) when multiple tunnel types are available for next-hop resolution.
