To configure BGP to use the segment routing tunnel in the tunnel table submitted by the lowest preference OSPFv3 instance for next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnels
            family ipv6
                resolution-filter
                    bgp
                    sr-isis
                    sr-ospf3
                    preference 200
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables BGP next-hop resolution using segment routing tunnels (sr-isis and sr-ospf3)
2. Sets a higher preference value (200) to ensure OSPFv3-installed tunnels are preferred over other tunnel types
3. Includes BGP tunnels as a fallback option

Note: You may need to adjust the preference value based on your specific network requirements to ensure OSPFv3-installed tunnels are indeed the lowest preference.
