## User question:
How to enable BGP to advertise locally configured non-local segment routing policies to BGP peers supporting the SR policy IPv4 address family on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP to advertise locally configured non-local segment routing policies to BGP peers supporting the SR policy IPv4 address family on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    family sr-policy-ipv4
exit
```

This command adds support for the SR Policy IPv4 address family (AFI1/SAFI73) in the BGP configuration, allowing the router to advertise segment routing policies to peers that support this address family.
