## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP on a Nokia router to advertise locally configured non-local segment routing policies as originated routes to BGP peers supporting the SR policy IPv4 address family, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    autonomous-system <your-AS-number>
    group <group-name>
        family sr-policy ipv4
        neighbor <peer-IP-address>
            peer-as <peer-AS-number>
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<your-AS-number>`, `<group-name>`, `<peer-IP-address>`, and `<peer-AS-number>` with your specific values. This configuration:
1. Enables BGP with your AS number
2. Creates a BGP group with SR Policy IPv4 address family support
3. Configures the BGP neighbor with the peer's AS number

The `family sr-policy ipv4` command enables the Segment Routing Policy IPv4 address family, allowing advertisement of SR policies to the specified peers.
