To enable segment routing policies for resolving BGP next hops of certain routes in Nokia routers, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunn family ipv4
            resolution-filter
                sr-policy
                sr-isis
        exit
        shortcut-tunn family ipv6
            resolution-filter
                sr-policy
                sr-isis
        exit
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel family ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    sr-policy
                    sr-isis
            exit
            transport-tunnel family ipv6
                resolution-filter
                    sr-policy
                    sr-isis
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables SR policies for both IPv4 and IPv6 BGP next-hop resolution under shortcut tunnels
2. Enables SR policies for labeled routes (both IPv4 and IPv6)
3. Includes SR-ISIS as a fallback mechanism for next-hop resolution

For specific route families, you can modify the configuration by including only the relevant address families (ipv4 or ipv6) as needed.
