To enable BGP next-hop resolution using segment routing policies for labeled IPv4 routes in Nokia routers, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        bgp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BGP next-hop resolution context
2. Configures labeled route options
3. Specifies transport tunnel settings for labeled IPv4 routes
4. Enables BGP tunneling for next-hop resolution of labeled IPv4 routes

The `bgp` command under `resolution-filter` enables the use of BGP-labeled routes (specifically segment routing policies) for next-hop resolution of labeled IPv4 prefixes.
