Here are the CLI commands to configure a BMP monitoring station named "NYC-DC1" on a Nokia router:

```
configure
    bmp
        station "NYC-DC1" create
            report-local-routes
            connection
                station-address <ip-address> port <port>
                local-address <ip-address>
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<ip-address>` with the actual IP address of your BMP monitoring station and `<port>` with the appropriate TCP port number. Optionally, specify the local-address if you want the router to use a specific source IP for communication with the BMP station.

To associate this BMP station with BGP monitoring (optional):
```
configure
    router
        bgp
            monitor
                station "NYC-DC1"
            exit
        exit
    exit
```
