Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure your Nokia router to send BMP messages to the monitoring stations "NYC-DC1" and "LON-DC2":

```
configure
    bmp
        station "NYC-DC1" create
            report-local-routes
            connection
                station-address <NYC-DC1-IP> port <port-number>
                connect-retry 120
                router <router-instance>
                local-address <local-ip-address>
            exit
        exit
        station "LON-DC2" create
            report-local-routes
            connection
                station-address <LON-DC2-IP> port <port-number>
                connect-retry 120
                router <router-instance>
                local-address <local-ip-address>
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace the following placeholders with your actual values:
- `<NYC-DC1-IP>` and `<LON-DC2-IP>` with the respective IP addresses of your monitoring stations
- `<port-number>` with the TCP port number (default is typically 11019)
- `<router-instance>` with your router instance name (e.g., "Base")
- `<local-ip-address>` with your router's local IP address to use for the connections
