To configure TCP keepalive parameters for the station on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure
bmp
station "station-name" 
connection
tcp-keepalive
keep-idle 600
keep-interval 15
keep-count 4
exit all
```

These commands set the TCP keepalive idle time to 600 seconds, the interval between probes to 15 seconds, and the number of missed keepalives before declaring the connection down to 4. Adjust the values as needed for your specific requirements.
