How to configure the tertiary IPv4 address as 192.0.2.10 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the tertiary IPv4 address 192.0.2.10 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    cluster 192.0.2.10 orr-location 3
exit
```

This configuration sets the cluster ID to 192.0.2.10 and assigns it as an optimal route reflection location with index 3 (tertiary). The `orr-location` parameter ensures routes are optimized for this specific location.
