To configure the tertiary IPv6 address 2001:db8::3 as a reference location for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    cluster 192.0.2.1 orr-location 3
exit
```

Note: Replace `192.0.2.1` with your actual cluster ID (typically one of the router's loopback addresses). The `orr-location 3` parameter associates this configuration with the third location (tertiary) where the IPv6 address 2001:db8::3 would be used as the reference point for optimal route reflection.
