To configure Nokia routers to only accept incoming BGP packets with a TTL value of at least 64, use the following CLI commands:

For EBGP peers:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> multihop 64
```

For IBGP peers (default is already 64):
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> multihop 64
```

These commands will ensure that BGP packets must have a TTL of at least 64 to be accepted by the router. The configuration can be applied at the global BGP level, group level, or individual neighbor level depending on your requirements.
