To configure your Nokia router to only accept incoming BGP packets with a TTL value of at least 64, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        ttl-security 64
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            ttl-security 64
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address if applying to a specific neighbor. This ensures BGP will only accept packets with TTL values ≥ 64.
