Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure BGP next-hop resolution for labeled routes to use UDP transport tunnels on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        udp
                    exit
                exit
                family ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        udp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables UDP transport tunnels for next-hop resolution of both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes under BGP.
