## User question:
"How to configure Nokia routers to handle BGP UPDATE message errors in a non-disruptive manner when no length errors prevent NLRI field parsing?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to handle BGP UPDATE message errors in a non-disruptive manner when no length errors prevent NLRI field parsing, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp error-handling
    update-fault-tolerance
exit
```

This enables the `treat-as-withdraw` behavior for UPDATE message errors while ensuring NLRI fields can still be parsed correctly.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
update-fault-tolerance
no update-fault-tolerance
FuncDef:
This command enablestreat-as-withdrawand other similarly non-disruptive approaches for handling a wide range of UPDATE message errors, as long as there are no length errors that prevent all of the NLRI fields from being correctly identified and parsed.
