Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure Nokia routers to apply base instance BGP export route policies to VPN-related routes including vpn-ipv4/6 and evpn, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    vpn-apply-export
exit
```

This command enables the application of base instance BGP export route policies to VPN-related routes (vpn-ipv4, vpn-ipv6, and evpn) at the global BGP level. 

If you need to apply this setting to specific BGP groups or neighbors instead, use:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    vpn-apply-export
exit
```

or

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    vpn-apply-export
exit
```
