This command configures the add-paths capability for VPN-IPv4 routes. By default, add-paths is not enabled for VPN-IPv4 routes.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'send-limit', 'Info': 'Specifies the maximum number of paths per VPN-IPv4 NLRI that are allowed to be advertised to add-paths peers (the actual number of advertised routes may be less depending on the next-hop diversity requirement, other configuration options, route policies and/or route advertisement rules). Values-1 to 16, none.'}
{'Parameters': 'receive', 'Info': 'Specifies that the router negotiates the add-paths receive capability for VPN-IPv4 routes with its peers.'}
{'Parameters': 'none', 'Info': 'Specifies that the router does not negotiate the Add-Paths receive capability for VPN-IPv4 routes with its peers.'}
